    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d416-a1">

                <pb facs="0640" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg540"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    318—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Aarifi Pasha to Mr.
                            Wallace.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Sublime Porte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 26,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">circular note verbale.</hi></p>
                <p>It appears from a communication received from the Department of the Interior that
                    foreigners living at Makrikeny refuse to allow themselves to be inscribed on the
                    census register until their consulates invite them to submit themselves to the
                    formality.</p>
                <p>In bringing this fact before the legation of the United States of America, the
                    ministry of foreign affairs begs it to be good enough to instruct whom it may
                    concern so that the American citizens established in the locality above
                    mentioned may no longer object to the census.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
